msgid "Sport Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:7
#: 2560c46495864d3ea1b65d4a2877a75f
msgid "Sport Mode is also known as \"rate controlled stabilize\" plus Altitude Hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:10
#: b2434c8e028a4a9d98a71f0d9c148cbd
msgid "this mode is not included by default in the firmware built and available on the `Firmware Server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ . Either the user must build his own firmware with this mode enabled or use the `Custom Firmware Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:13
#: 83760e00e24d492aa563f9ce51d71108
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:15
#: a594f5b63eaa4ac4b3437fbc52ba15ce
msgid "It was designed to be useful for flying FPV and filming `dolly shots <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolly_shot>`__ or fly bys because you can set the vehicle at a particular angle and it will maintain that angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:18
#: b7fcbcfb192245bd8732eb24b11ec196
msgid "The pilot's roll, pitch and yaw sticks control the rate of rotation of the vehicle so when the sticks are released the vehicle will remain in its current attitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:21
#: d81b8ce96c814728abc4e4016d41a3a0
msgid "The vehicle will not lean more than 30 degrees (this angle is adjustable with the :ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>` parameter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sport-mode.rst:23
#: 8710fb421a4f43938e84b2691cd9c0cf
msgid "The altitude is maintained with the altitude hold controller so the vehicle will attempt to hold its current altitude when the sticks are within the mid-throttle deadzone, which is adjustable with :ref:`THR_DZ<THR_DZ>`. It will climb or descend at up to 2.5m/s (this speed is adjustable with the :ref:`PILOT_SPD_UP<PILOT_SPD_UP>` and :ref:`PILOT_SPD_DN<PILOT_SPD_DN>` parameters). The acceleration used to establish these speeds is set by :ref:`PILOT_ACC_Z<PILOT_ACC_Z>`."
msgstr ""
